  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Calculate the distance between the points $(3w,2w,7w)$ and $(-w,6w,3w),$ given that $w$ is positive.",
  "worked_solution": "The distance $d$ between two points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1}{)}^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1}{)}^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1}{)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have ${{(3w,2w,7w)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,\u00a0}{y}_{1}\\text{,\u00a0}{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and ${{(-w,6w,3w)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,\u00a0}{y}_{2}\\text{,\u00a0}{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Applying the distance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(-w-3w{)}^{2}+(6w-2w{)}^{2}+(3w-7w{)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4w{)}^{2}+(4w{)}^{2}+(-4w{)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{w}^{2}+16{w}^{2}+16{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48}\\,\\sqrt{{w}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\,|w|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $w$ is positive, we have $|w|=w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nd=4\\sqrt{3}\\,w.\n$$",
